<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.3.1: Quadratic Expressions and Area</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01776</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.3.1: Quadratic Expressions and Area</md:title>
    <md:uuid>9b2c88ca-c376-45d5-b27a-d3ca582c425f</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Figure A is a large square. Figure B is a large square with a smaller square removed. Figure C is composed of two large squares with one smaller square added.</para>
      <para id="para-00002">Figure A</para>
      <para id="para-00003">
          <media alt="A square.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_05_02_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        
     </para>
      <para id="para-00004">Figure B</para>
      <para id="para-00005">
          <media alt="A square with a 1 by 1 square removed from the lower left interior.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_05_02_02.svg"/>
          </media>
        
     </para>
      <para id="para-00006">Figure C</para>
      <para id="para-00007">
          <media alt="Two large squares connected on the right side to a one by one smaller square.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_05_02_03.svg"/>
          </media>
        
     </para>
      <para id="para-00008">Write an expression to represent the area of each shaded figure when the side length of the large square is as shown in the first column.</para>
      <para id="para-00009">Copy and complete the table. Compare your work by answering 1 - 12.</para>
      <table class="unnumbered os-raise-wideequaltable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="4">
<<<<<<< HEAD
          <tbody>
=======
        
  <tbody>
>>>>>>> a9b3d22748ccf4d962d8f71574c293c2a589b83c
            <row>
              <entry>
                <emphasis> Side length of large square </emphasis>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <emphasis> Area of A </emphasis>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <emphasis> Area of B </emphasis>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <emphasis> Area of C </emphasis>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00010"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></entry>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00011"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></entry>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00012"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></para></entry>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00013"><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></para></entry>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
              <entry/>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00014">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure A?</para>
          <para id="para-00015">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00016">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00017"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00018">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure B?</para>
          <para id="para-00019">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00020">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00021"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00003">
          <para id="para-00022">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure C?</para>
          <para id="para-00023">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00003">
          <para id="para-00024">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00025"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:msup><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00004">
          <para id="para-00026">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure A?</para>
          <para id="para-00027">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00004">
          <para id="para-00028">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00029"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00005">
        <problem id="prob-00005">
          <para id="para-00030">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure B?</para>
          <para id="para-00031">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00005">
          <para id="para-00032">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00033"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00006">
          <para id="para-00034">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure C?</para>
          <para id="para-00035">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00006">
          <para id="para-00036">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00037"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00007">
          <para id="para-00038">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure A?</para>
          <para id="para-00039">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00007">
          <para id="para-00040">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00041"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00008">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00042">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure B?</para>
          <para id="para-00043">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00044">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00045"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>16</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00009">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00046">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure C?</para>
          <para id="para-00047">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00048">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00049"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>32</m:mn><m:msup><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00010">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00050">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure A?</para>
          <para id="para-00051">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00052">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00053"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup></m:mrow></m:math> or <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00011">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00054">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure B?</para>
          <para id="para-00055">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00056">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00057"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00012">
        <problem id="prob-00012">
          <para id="para-00058">When the side length of the large square is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the area of figure C</para>
          <para id="para-00059">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00012">
          <para id="para-00060">Compare your answer: </para>
          <para id="para-00061"><m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:msup><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:msup><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> (or an equivalent expression)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
